# Modular code

Screens compose. They do not own large UI trees or domain logic.

Ponytail still wins on size: extract at a real boundary, not a speculative layer. No empty folders. No one-function-per-file.

- Route files (`app/**`) stay thin: session/mock, RBAC gate, compose feature components.
- Feature UI lives in `components/<feature>/` (`hub/`, `inbox/`, `chat/`). Create the folder when the first real component lands.
- RNR primitives stay in `components/ui/` only. Never put app UI there.
- Domain helpers, filters, formatters live in `lib/` with their test beside them.
- Extract when reused in 2+ places, or when a file is doing more than one job.
- Do not extract one-off wrappers, 10-line single-use fragments, or a catch-all `utils/` dump.
- One concern per module: inbox row ≠ thread bubble ≠ composer.

Import direction (no reverse): `app/**` → `components/*` + `lib/*` → `components/ui` has no feature imports; `lib/*` has no RN UI.

```tsx
// BAD — route owns header, bubbles, composer, send, RBAC
export default function ChatScreen() { /* 200 lines */ }

// GOOD
// app/chat/[id].tsx — gate + compose
// components/chat/thread-header.tsx
// components/chat/message-list.tsx
// components/chat/composer.tsx
```
